KZ3 patch 4031 (network pass 16): ENHANCEMENT, off by default. Autocomplete of the motion sections (valve, charge), the
opt-in button combo. Setting: keybinds.ini `[motion] autocomplete = off|hold` (default off; bridge command
"autocomplete [off|hold]" like "dsu"). Trigger: both stick clicks (L3 + R3) held for 0.5 s while a human controller is
in a valve or charge section, read from the pad packet after the bindings (a keyboard gets it through whatever keys are
bound to L3 and R3: LeftShift + V or Mouse2 with the default keys; L1+R1 is avoided, KZ2 uses it). Outside the
sections nothing is read. The post-hooks of patch 4030 (ValveJoystickController::Update 1.14 0x61AEB4; charge target
0x6126E4) then overwrite the controller's own outputs after the game computed them: valve target +0x108 (and the
follower's previous +0x114) and the grab gains +0x10C/+0x110 (0.0 held / 1.0 released), charge target +0x108 (previous
+0x118) and grab byte +0x114. The valve is driven through the game's ratchet (push to the hand limit with the grab
held, return with it released, wrong-way detection flips the direction) until the valve position n reaches
DisableValue's side; the charge alternates the ArmRanges window centres. The game's own completion (disable call
0x5CA6D0, sounds, animation, Lua M_GetValveValue, checkpoint) runs unchanged; no script is skipped. Release the combo
and the game's own controls are back at once. Values: ValveResource Valve_CounterClockwise_AutoDisable (hand -35..35,
speed 360, Min 0, Max 200, Initial 180, DisableValue 0), ISA_D_Charge (windows +-0.7854 rad, ArmStepTime 0).
Logs: "[assist] L3+R3 held 0.5 s", "[assist] combo held: valve autocomplete engaged", "[assist] valve sweep push",
"[assist] valve done n=". Host test: tools/smoke/test_motion_assist.sh.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 153): hunks unchanged; offsets and context follow the v0.19.0 chain (group A r152 files, Toro v019-c, R&C v019-b where delivered; originals for the rest, three-way merged where they did not apply).

